  <static seed="139" source="Library/Valdosta/APEX_Calculus/2.4/APEX_2.4_16.pg">
    <statement><p>Compute the derivative of the given function.</p>
<p><me>f(t) = \frac{1}{t^{3}} \left( \tan t + 8 \right)</me></p>
<p><m>f'(t) =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>t^{-3}\sec^{2}\mathopen{}\left(t\right)+\left(-3\right)t^{-4}\mathopen{}\left(\tan\mathopen{}\left(t\right)+8\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



Use the Product Rule.



<me>f'(t) = (t^{-3})(\sec^2 t) + (-3 t^{-4})(\tan t + 8).</me>


</solution>
